INT. FERRY TERMINAL - WAITING ROOM - EARLY MORNING

Plastic benches bolted in rows. A vending machine glowing blue. A departures board reads CANCELLED in red beside every sailing. Fog presses at the windows like a hand.

PERPETUA OSEI-ADJEI (60s, camel coat, a small suitcase between her feet) sits alone with her purse on her lap. She has not taken off her gloves.

She watches the board. She watches the door. She watches nothing.

A clock ticks, loud in the silence. A gull lands on the sill, regards her, and leaves.

The door opens. Cold air. A MAN steps in, shaking out a wet umbrella: JULIAN OSEI-ADJEI (30s, her son, scarf, luggage on wheels). He sees her and stops dead.

JULIAN
Mother.

PERPETUA
You came.

JULIAN
You said the 6:15.

PERPETUA
It's cancelled.

JULIAN
I saw the board.

He crosses to the vending machine. He studies it without buying.

PERPETUA
They say it will clear by noon.

JULIAN
They always say that.

He sits, one bench away. He sets the umbrella down. It drips on the linoleum between them.

PERPETUA
Your father would have liked the fog.

JULIAN
Would he.

PERPETUA
He said fog was honest. Everything looks the way it feels.

Julian says nothing. He picks at the handle of his suitcase.

JULIAN
Did you eat?

PERPETUA
A little.

JULIAN
What did you eat?

PERPETUA
Toast.

JULIAN
That isn't a meal.

PERPETUA
It is if you are me.

He almost smiles. He rises, crosses to the vending machine, feeds a coin. A packet drops. He brings it to her. Biscuits.

She takes them, turns the packet over, reads the ingredients as though they were a letter.

PERPETUA (CONT'D)
Too much sugar.

JULIAN
Eat them anyway.

She opens the packet. She eats one. She offers him the packet. He takes one. They chew in silence.

JULIAN (CONT'D)
When did you last visit the grave?

PERPETUA
Sunday.

JULIAN
I haven't been in a year.

PERPETUA
I know.

JULIAN
I didn't know what to say to him.

PERPETUA
He wouldn't have talked back.

JULIAN
That's the problem.

A soft laugh. She folds the packet and tucks it into her purse. The loudspeaker clicks on: a bored recorded voice announces a one-hour delay.

JULIAN (CONT'D)
One hour.

PERPETUA
One hour.

JULIAN
We could go.

PERPETUA
Where?

JULIAN
The grave. It's ten minutes by taxi.

She looks at him. Her gloved hands tighten on the purse. Her eyes go to the window, where the fog is thinning.

PERPETUA
I'll need to freshen my lipstick.

JULIAN
Take your time.

She stands. She straightens her coat. She picks up her small suitcase, and he, without being asked, takes it from her hand.

They walk to the door together. At the threshold he holds it open, and she goes through first, into the gray.
